# Commits

Every commit follows Conventional Commits: `type(scope): description`.

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `style`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`, `perf`.
- Scope is optional and names the area: `tenancy`, `auth`, `admin`, `posts`, `blog`, `media`, `queue`, `cache`, `branding`, `deps`.
- Description is lowercase, imperative, no trailing period, under 72 characters.
- One logical change per commit. Tests may ship with the change they cover.
- Never add AI attribution, `Co-authored-by` or "Generated with" lines.

```text
# Good
feat(posts): add scheduled status to post form
fix(tenancy): pin queue jobs table to the central connection

# Bad
Updated stuff
feat: Added posts CRUD, images and caching.
```

# Branches and pull requests

- One feature per branch, named `feat/<feature>` (or `fix/`, `chore/`).
- PR description has three sections: **What changed**, **Why**, **How I tested**.
- CI must be green before requesting review. Authors never merge their own PRs.
